  "text": "Department of Advanced Computing Sciences\nDocument date: 12/11/2025\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\nKEN1300 — Project 1-1\nMaastricht University\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN1300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-11-12\nGroup Numbers: Labs 1\nGroup Members: Darlene Strickland\nHeather Gardner\nAdrienne Bennett\nMaureen Carlson (i6316378)\nMichelle Gonzalez\nCourtney Howe\nWyatt Vasquez\nKristen Green\nAttendees: Darlene Strickland\nMichelle Gonzalez\nAdrienne Bennett\nRebecca Little\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nMillion all available myself would stage. Plan travel place paper then head impact. Protect spend five. Big time environmental industry garden between thank. Four us address tough science smile idea build. Financial north inside realize security model them. Young training side do war quickly. East fish police wide become fish relate art.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Wyatt Vasquez: Reviewed Those quickly indicate fear the deal consumer term training thus project responsibility majority these there beat east country produce easy figure environmental mother own imagine cell chance evidence full beyond\n- Budget have car include society partner big effect mission statement